$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: α -ORGANOSULFONYLOXYLATION: GENERAL PROCEDURE
Alcohol (5 mmol) was added in one portion to a stirred suspension of
Dess-Martin periodinane (15 mmol) and organosulfonic acid (15 mmol) in
CH3CN (20mL), and the reaction mixture was refluxed for 4 h. Solvent was
removed under reduced pressure, and the residue obtained was diluted by
adding CHCl3 (60 mL) and washed with saturated solution of NaHCO3 (2 x 35
mL) and brine (60 mL). The organic layer was dried over anhydrous Na2SO4
and concentrated under reduced pressure to give crude α
-organosulfonyloxylated product. Pure product was obtained after column
chromatography (SiO2, mesh size 60-120, eluent, ethyl acetate-hexane,
15:85). Table 2. Entry 6, yield 74%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM One-Pot Protocol for Synthesis of α-Organosulfonyloxy Ketones from
Secondary Alcohols Using Hypervalent Iodine(V)-Mediated Oxidations
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Deshmukh, Swapnil S.; Huddar, Sameerana N.; Akamanchi, Krishnacharya G.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2009), 39(17), 3101-3110

