$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(2):CAS_RN
$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Dess-Martin Oxidation of 1; General Procedure
To a solution of amino acid derivative 1 (1.0 mmol) in anhydrous CH2Cl2
(10 mL), Dess-Martin periodinane (636 mg, 1.5 mmol) was added at 0 °C
under nitrogen and the mixture was stirred at r.t. After the reaction was
complete, the reaction was quenched with sat. NaHCO3 (5 mL) containing
Na2S2O3 (5 mmol) and the mixture was extracted with CH2Cl2 (2 × 10 mL).
The organic layers were washed with brine (15 mL), dried over Na2SO4 and
the solvent was removed in vacuo. The corresponding aldehyde 7 was
obtained after column chromatography (silica gel gel; EtOAc-hexane).
tert-Butyl 4-Oxo-3-phenyl-2-(2,2,2-trifluoroacetamido)butanoate (7a)
According to the general procedure for Dess-Martin oxidations, 1a (347
mg, 1.0 mmol, dr = 75:25) and Dess-Martin periodinane (636 mg, 1.5 mmol)
were allowed to react to give 7a after flash chromatography (silica gel;
hexanes-EtOAc, 8:2) as a mixture of diastereomers (dr = 75:25). Yield:
66% (228 mg, 0.66 mmol); tert-Butyl
3-(2-Chlorophenyl)-4-oxo-2-(2,2,2-trifluoroacetamido)butanoate (7c)
According to the general procedure for Dess-Martin oxidations, 1e (382
mg, 1.0 mmol, dr = 75:25) and Dess-Martin periodinane (636 mg, 1.5 mmol)
were allowed to react to give 7c after flash chromatography (silica gel;
hexanes-EtOAc, 8:2) as a mixture of diastereomers (dr = 75:25). Yield:
73% (277 mg, 0.73 mmol); colorless oil. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ [major
diastereomer (syn)] = 9.68 (s, 1 H, 4-H), 7.27-7.33 (m, 4 H), 6.78 (d, J
= 7.4 Hz, 1 H), 4.88 (dd, J = 7.5, 3.9 Hz, 1 H), 4.80 (d, J = 4.0 Hz, 1
H), 1.48 (s, 9 H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ [major diastereomer (syn)]
= 199.5, 167.7, 156.9 (q, J = 37.5 Hz), 138.9, 131.6, 128.9, 128.7,
127.2, 126.4, 115.5 (q, J = 285.9 Hz), 83.7, 55.8, 52.0, 27.6. 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3): δ [minor diastereomer (anti, selected signals)] = 9.75
(s, 1 H), 6.87 (d, J = 7.9 Hz, 1 H), 5.09 (dd, J = 8.4, 6.4 Hz, 1 H),
4.47 (d, J = 6.6 Hz, 1 H), 1.44 (s, 9 H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ
[minor diastereomer (anti, selected signals)] = 196.9, 167.8, 137.9,
131.5, 129.6, 129.4, 128.7, 84.1, 56.2, 52.2, 27.7. HRMS (CI): m/z [M]+
calcd for C16H17ClF3NO4: 379.0798; found: 379.0786.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Dess-Martin oxidation, reactant taken as diastereomeric mixture (dr
75:25)
