$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a stirred solution of the alcohol (4.59 g, 14.0 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (250
mL) was added manganese (IV) oxide (<5 μm particle size, 85%, 12.39 g,
121 mmol, 8.7 mol equiv) and the mixture was stirred overnight at room
temperature. The mixture was filtered through Celite and the cake was
washed with CH2Cl2. Concentration of the filtrate followed by
purification on silica gel (97:3 CH2Cl2/MeOH) afforded the aldehyde 16 as
a pale yellow oil (3.27 g, 72%). 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 1.45 (s, 9H), 4.48-4.63
(m, 4H), 7.16-7.26 (m, 4H), 7.65 (td, 1H, J = 7.7, 1.5 Hz), 7.83 (d, 2H,
9.0 Hz), 8.53 (d, 1H, J = 4.5 Hz), 9.99 (s, 1H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of Novel Small Molecule Orally Bioavailable C-X-C Chemokine
Receptor 4 Antagonists That Are Potent Inhibitors of T-Tropic (X4) HIV-1
Replication
