$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To homoallylic alcohol 15 (158 mg, 0.29 mmol) in THF (2.9 mL, 0.1 M) at 0
°C was added AcOH (21 mg, 0.35 mmol) and TBAF (1 M solution in THF, 0.32
mL, 0.32 mmol). The reaction mixture was stirred at 25 °C for 24 h, at
which point it was quenched with saturated aqueous NaHCO3. The mixture
was extracted with Et2O for three times and the combined organic
fractions were dried over Na2SO4, and concentrated in vacuo. The residue
was run through a quick column chromatography (SiO2; ethyl
acetate:hexanes, 1:10 to 1:4) to provide 101 mg crude hemi-acetal 15a as
a mixture of four diastereomers. A solution of 101 mg crude hemi-acetal
15a in CH2Cl2 (2.5 mL) was added slowly to a solution of Dess-Martin
periodinane (200 mg, 0.47 mmol), NaHCO3 (99 mg, 1.17 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (2.5
mL, 0.05 M) at 0 °C. The reaction was stirred at 25 °C for 3 h, at which
point it was quenched with pH 7 phosphate buffer. The mixture was
extracted with CH2Cl2 for three times and the combined organic fractions
were dried over Na2SO4, and concentrated in vacuo. The residue was
purified by column chromatography (SiO2; ethyl acetate:hexanes, 1:8 to
1:4) to provide β,γ- enone 16 (89 mg, 0.21 mmol) as a colorless oil in
72% yield over 2 steps. 16, yield (89 mg, 0.21 mmol, 72%). 1H NMR (400
MHz, CDCl3): δ 5.93-5.83 (m, 1H), 5.50 (dd, J = 8.8, 2.4 Hz, 1H),
5.15-5.07 (m, 2H), 4.22-4.08 (m, 2H), 3.38-3.25 (m, 2H), 2.76 (dd, J =
17.2, 6.0 Hz, 1H), 2.39 (dd, J = 17.2, 7.6 Hz, 1H), 2.08-2.01 (m, 1H),
2.04 (s, 3H), 1.83-1.72 (m, 2H), 1.70-1.58 (m, 1H), 1.16 (s, 3H), 1.11
(s, 3H), 0.86 (s, 9H), 0.05 (s, 6H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 210.6,
170.2, 169.7, 130.8, 118.2, 73.6, 72.9, 64.2, 51.5, 42.3, 39.8, 38.3,
37.0, 25.5, 20.8, 20.6, 19.8, 17.8, -4.9. FTIR (neat): ν 2954, 2930,
2857, 1740, 1708, 1472, 1390, 1370, 1240, 1085, 1061, 836 cm-1. HRMS (CI)
Calcd. for C22H39O6Si [M+H]+: 427.2516, Found: 427.2510. [α]25 D: -10.0°
(c = 1.00, CH2Cl2). TLC (SiO2): Rf = 0.55 (ethyl acetate:hexanes, 1:2).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM buffered soln. in last stage/phosphate
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Total synthesis of bryostatin 7 via C-C bond-forming hydrogenation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Lu, Yu; Woo, Sang Kook; Krische, Michael J.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2011), 133(35), 13876-13879

