$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of ONE (2). Dess-Martin periodinane (1.8 g, 4.3 mmol) was added
to a solution of 1 (0.52 g, 3.3 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (16 mL). After 30 min,
the reaction mixture was concentrated and purified by column
chromatography (10% EtOAc/hexanes). The product (0.37 g) was isolated as
a yellow oil in 72% yield. The NMR data was consistent with the
literature.25 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 9.74 (d, 1H, J = 7.0 Hz), 6.85 (d, 1H, J =
16.2 Hz), 6.73 (dd, 1H, J = 7.0, 16.3 Hz), 2.65 (t, 2H, J = 7.3 Hz), 1.62
(m, 2H), 1.30-1.27 (m, 4H), 0.86 (t, 3H, J = 6.8 Hz); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 2
00.1, 193.4, 144.9, 137.2, 41.1, 31.2, 23.3, 22.3, 13.8.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM literature preparation, Dess-Martin oxidation
