$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 8-Formyl-cyclodec-3-ene-1,5-diyne •2[Co2(CO)6] (57) Oxalyl chloride (32.4
μL, 47.1 mg, 0.3714 mmol) was dissolved in CH2Cl2 (1.0 mL) and the
solution was cooled to -78°C. A solution of DMSO (52.6 μL, 57.9 mg,
0.7412 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (1 mL) was then added dropwise and the resulting
mixture was stirred at -78°C for 0.5 h before a solution of alcohol 55
(123 mg, 0.1684 mmol) in CH2Cl2(1 mL) was added dropwise. The resulting
solution was stirred at -78°C for 1.0 h., Et3N (236 μl, 171 mg, 1.69
mmol) added, stirring continued for 3.0 hat -78°C, then the cooling bath
removed and the mixture was allowed to warm to 0°C. After 1.0 h at 0°C,
the mixture was poured into water(20 mL) and extracted with CH2Cl2 (3 x
10 mL). The combined organic extracts were washed with HCl (10%, 2 x 10
mL), saturated NaHCO3 (20 mL), and brine (20 mL), then dried over MgSO4,
filtered through a plug of silica, and concentrated in vacuo. Column
chromatography (silica gel, 95:5 hexane:EtOAc) afforded 88.5 mg (72 %) of
the title compound as a dark green foam.
8-Formyl-cyclodec-3-ene-1,5-diyne •2[Co2(CO)6] (57), 88.5 mg (72 %) yield
1H NMR: δ 9.72 (s, 1H), 6.35 (s, 2H), 3.25 (m, 4H), 2.72 (m, 1H), 2.05
(m, 2H); 13C NMR: δ 200.6, 198.9, 125.6, 95.1, 94.6, 83.5, 82.7, 53.3,
32.3, 31.2, 29.3; Analysis calcd for C23H10O13Co4: C, 37.94; H, 1.38;
found C, 38.23; H, 1.01.
