$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Dess-Martin Oxidation of 1; General Procedure To a solution of amino acid
derivative 1 (1.0 mmol) in anhydrous CH2Cl2 (10 mL), Dess-Martin
periodinane (636 mg, 1.5 mmol) was added at 0 °C under nitrogen and the
mixture was stirred at r.t. After the reaction was complete, the reaction
was quenched with sat. NaHCO3 (5 mL) containing Na2S2O3 (5 mmol) and the
mixture was extracted with CH2Cl2 (2 × 10 mL). The organic layers were
washed with brine (15 mL), dried over Na2SO4 and the solvent was removed
in vacuo. The corresponding aldehyde 7 was obtained after column
chromatography (silica gel gel; EtOAc-hexane). tert-Butyl
4-Oxo-3-phenyl-2-(2,2,2-trifluoroacetamido)butanoate (7a) According to
the general procedure for Dess-Martin oxidations, 1a (347 mg, 1.0 mmol,
dr = 75:25) and Dess-Martin periodinane (636 mg, 1.5 mmol) were allowed
to react to give 7a after flash chromatography (silica gel;
hexanes-EtOAc, 8:2) as a mixture of diastereomers (dr = 75:25). Yield:
66% (228 mg, 0.66 mmol); Yield 71%, colorless oil. 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3): δ [major diastereomer (syn)] = 9.76 (s, 1 H), 7.38-7.45 (m, 5 H),
7.10 (d, J = 8.3 Hz, 1 H), 4.98 (dd, J = 9.2, 4.3 Hz, 1 H), 4.52 (d, J =
4.4 Hz, 1 H), 1.47 (s, 9 H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ [major
diastereomer (syn)] = 198.7, 167.5, 156.9 (q, J = 37.5 Hz), 130.9, 129.5,
129.3, 128.8, 115.6 (q, J = 285.6 Hz), 84.0, 59.1, 53.0, 27.7. 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3): δ [minor diastereomer (anti, selected signals)] = 9.85
(s, 1 H), 7.15-7.22 (m, 5 H), 6.70 (d, J = 7.5 Hz, 1 H), 5.14 (dd, J =
8.3, 5.5 Hz, 1 H), 4.30 (d, J = 5.4 Hz, 1 H), 1.48 (s, 9 H). 13C NMR (100
MHz, CDCl3): δ [minor diastereomer (anti, selected signals)] = 196.7,
168.7, 167.6, 131.1, 129.6, 129.3, 128.3, 84.3, 59.4, 53.6, 27.8. HRMS
(CI): m/z [M + 1]+ calcd for C16H18F3NO4: 346.1221; found: 346.1253.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Dess-Martin oxidation, reactant taken as diastereomeric mixture (dr
75:25)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A straightforward synthetic approach to β-substituted phenylalanines via
ring opening of aryl epoxides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Zahoor, Ameer F.; Kazmaier, Uli
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2011), (7), 1059-1066

