$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure D for Dess-Martin Oxidation. To a solution of alcohol
in CH2Cl2 was added Dess-Martin periodinane (3.0 equiv). After being
stirred for 1 h, the reaction mixture was diluted with CH2Cl2 and sodium
thiosulfate solution (10%) was added. The mixture was stirred for 10 min
and extracted with CH2Cl2. The organic layer was washed with saturated
NaHCO3 solution, dried over MgSO4, and concentrated under reduced
pressure. The residue was purified by flash column chromatography on
silica gel (EtOAc/n-hexane = 1:6 to 1:2) to afford the corresponding
oxidized product. The aldehyde 41 (11 mg, 71%) was prepared from the
above alcohol according to the general procedure D and was purified by
flash column chromatography on silica gel (EtOAc/n-hexane = 1:2) to
afford 11 mg (71%) of pure 41 as a colorless oil.
2-(3,4-Dimethoxyphenyl)-3-(4-methoxybenzyloxy)propanal. 1H NMR (CDCl3,300
MHz) δ 9.66 (d, 1H, J = 1.7 Hz), 7.14 (d, 1H, J = 8.4 Hz), 6.78 (m, 3H),
6.66 (m. 2H), 4.40 (d, 2H, J = 3.5 Hz), 3.99 (dd, 1H, J = 8.6, 6.9 Hz),
3.80 (s, 3H), 3.77 (s, 3H), 3.73 (s, 3H), 3.70 (m, 2H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Dess-Martin oxidation
